    "@id": "cm:interpersonal-conflict"
   },
   "skos:definition": "A conversation you are tempted to avoid because the topic threatens the relationship, the other person's or your own self-image, or strong feelings on either side - raising a performance problem, disagreeing with a decision, delivering bad news or repairing a falling-out. It goes best when approached as a shared attempt to learn what happened, not a contest over who is right.",
