   "rdfs:label": "Grice's cooperative principle",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "Grice's maxims",
    "Gricean maxims",
    "conversational maxims",
    "cooperative principle",
    "maxims of conversation"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "cm:pragmatics"
   },
   "skos:definition": "Philosopher Paul Grice's account of how conversation works: listeners assume a speaker is trying to contribute what the exchange needs, and expect contributions to be true (Quality), as informative as needed and no more (Quantity), relevant (Relation) and clear (Manner); departures from these expectations are read as signals of unstated meaning.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
