   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "cm:intercultural-communication"
   },
   "skos:definition": "Edward T. Hall's contrast between communication in which most meaning sits in shared context, relationships and nonverbal cues (high-context) and communication in which meaning is carried mainly by explicit words (low-context); widely taught for intercultural work, but its country rankings have weak empirical support.",
