    },
    {
     "@id": "cm:silence-and-pauses"
    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "Deliberately leaving a pause of a few seconds after you ask a question (wait time 1) and again after the other person finishes answering (wait time 2), so people have time to think and to add to what they said, instead of the conversation snapping to the fastest or loudest reply.",
