  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/1",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:self-distancing"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "If I described this moment to myself by name, what would I tell me to do next?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/2",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:self-distancing"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "From a colleague's seat, how much of this meeting is actually about me?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/3",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:self-distancing"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Am I replaying this slip in the first person, and what would an observer say mattered instead?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/check/4",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:self-distancing"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Have I turned the distanced view into one concrete next action?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/example",
   "@type": "cmo:Rewrite",
   "cmo:after": "Priya, picture this from the back of the room: eight people focused on their own slides. You spotted a real gap. Ask one short question about the churn assumption, then let the lead answer.",
   "cmo:before": "I'm going to sound naive. Everyone will remember that I'm the one who didn't get the model. I'll just keep quiet and email the lead later.",
   "cmo:situation": "An analyst is about to raise a concern about a vendor's numbers in a cross-team review where she is the most junior person.",
   "cmo:why": "Naming herself and taking an observer's view shrinks the imagined spotlight and turns vague dread into one specific, low-cost contribution, which is the pattern lab studies link to less distress and better performance."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Self-distancing strategies",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before the meeting or talk, write or say two or three sentences of self-talk using your own name or \"you\" instead of \"I\" (for example, \"Sam, you know this material; your job is to explain it\")."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Picture the room from the back row or from a colleague's seat, not through your own eyes, and ask what that observer would actually notice."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Notice what the observer is busy with - their own agenda, notes and next point - and adjust your estimate of how much attention you will get."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Turn the distanced view into one concrete action, such as the opening line, the one question you will ask or the one-sentence correction you will use if you slip."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, review the moment the same way (\"What did Sam do well? What would Sam change?\") instead of replaying it in the first person."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/check/1",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:setting-reply-time-expectations"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Does this message say when I need a reply, or would the reader have to guess?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/check/2",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:setting-reply-time-expectations"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Am I sending outside the recipient's working hours, and if so have I said it can wait or scheduled it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/check/3",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:setting-reply-time-expectations"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is the urgency I am signalling the urgency I actually have?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/check/4",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:setting-reply-time-expectations"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Would my team know our default reply window for this channel without asking?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/example",
   "@type": "cmo:Rewrite",
   "cmo:after": "Hi Sam - comments on the report below. No need to look at this before Monday; I need the revised version by Wednesday noon for Thursday's client meeting. Enjoy your weekend.",
   "cmo:before": "Hi Sam - a few comments on the report below. Can you take a look?",
   "cmo:situation": "A team lead reviewing a draft report on Saturday morning emails comments to an analyst; the comments are needed for a client meeting the following Thursday.",
   "cmo:why": "The original leaves Sam to guess whether a Saturday email means 'reply today'; the rewrite gives the real deadline and its reason and says the weekend is free, the kind of sender-side note that removed receivers' overestimate of urgency in experiments."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Setting reply-time expectations",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before sending, decide when you truly need an answer - a date and time, or \"no deadline\" - and whether you need a reply at all or the message is for information only."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "For real deadlines, state the reply-by time and the reason in the first lines or the subject line (for example \"[Action by Thu 3pm]\"), not only at the end."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For anything non-urgent, add one plain sentence saying so, especially when you send outside normal working hours or across time zones."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Reserve urgent labels for messages that genuinely need fast action, and use a phone call or chat ping for true emergencies instead of a late-night email."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "If you work odd hours, schedule-send to the recipient's working hours or add a standing signature line saying you do not expect replies outside them."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/setting-reply-time-expectations/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Agree default reply windows for each channel with your team (for example chat same day, email within two working days) and write them in the team charter so individual messages only need to flag exceptions."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/check/1",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:situation-behavior-impact"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Could the other person picture the exact moment I mean, or did I say something vague like \"lately\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/check/2",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:situation-behavior-impact"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is my behaviour description something a camera could record, or did I slip in a judgement or guess at a motive?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/check/3",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:situation-behavior-impact"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Have I said what the impact actually was, rather than assuming they already know?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/check/4",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:situation-behavior-impact"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I leave room to ask about their intent and listen before deciding what should change?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/example",
   "@type": "cmo:Rewrite",
   "cmo:after": "In this morning's quarterly review with the VPs, when Priya asked where the churn figure came from, you said 'I'd have to check' and moved on. The VPs then questioned two other numbers and we lost ten minutes of the agenda, and I was worried they'd discount the whole forecast. What was going on for you at that point?",
   "cmo:before": "You came across as really unprepared today and kind of defensive. You need to step up your game before the next one.",
   "cmo:situation": "A team lead gives feedback to an analyst who presented the quarterly numbers at a leadership review.",
   "cmo:why": "The rewrite swaps verdicts (\"unprepared\", \"defensive\") for a time-stamped situation, an observable behaviour and a concrete impact, then asks about intent - so the analyst can see exactly what to change and has room to explain instead of defending their character."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Situation-Behavior-Impact",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pin down the situation - the specific meeting, document or moment, with a time and place (\"in Tuesday's 10 a.m. client call\"), not \"lately\" or \"last week\"."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Describe the behaviour as something a camera could have recorded - words said, actions taken - and strip out labels such as \"rude\", \"lazy\" or \"great attitude\"."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "State the impact the behaviour had on you, the team or the work, in your own voice, naming a concrete consequence and, if useful, your reaction (frustrated, relieved, proud)."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "For redirecting feedback, stop and ask about intent (\"What were you aiming for there?\") and listen before proposing any fix."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Agree together on what to keep doing or what to try next time, and give the feedback close to the event while it is still fresh."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/situation-behavior-impact/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Use the same three parts for positive feedback, so the person knows exactly which behaviour to repeat."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/small-talk/check/1",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:small-talk"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I ask at least one follow-up question that built on something they actually said?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/small-talk/check/2",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:small-talk"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I share something about myself too, or did the exchange feel like an interview?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/small-talk/check/3",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:small-talk"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I go one step deeper than the weather or the commute when the moment allowed it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/small-talk/check/4",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:small-talk"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Was this a good time for them, or did I pull a focused colleague out of deep work?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/small-talk/check/5",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:small-talk"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I end the chat cleanly, with a warm close or a link back to the work?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/check/1",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:social-accounts"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Could the people affected repeat the actual reason for this outcome after hearing my explanation?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/check/2",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:social-accounts"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Have I named only causes that are true and that I would be comfortable having checked?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/check/3",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:social-accounts"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Did I explain how they will be treated from here, not only why it happened?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/check/4",
   "@type": "cmo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "cmo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "cm:social-accounts"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is my explanation a short context for an apology, or has it become an excuse that replaces one?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/example",
   "@type": "cmo:Rewrite",
   "cmo:after": "I have to take back the conference places I promised you. Q3 revenue came in 12% under plan, and finance has frozen all non-customer travel across the division until March - I argued to keep two places and lost that argument. Registrations will be refunded by Friday, so none of you are out of pocket, and I've booked 15 minutes with each of you this week to agree what we do instead for your development goals. If any part of that still doesn't add up, ask me directly.",
   "cmo:before": "Hi all, due to business reasons the conference budget has been cut for this year. Thanks for understanding.",
   "cmo:situation": "A team lead has to tell five analysts that the conference places she had promised them this year have been cancelled.",
   "cmo:why": "The vague original gives no reason anyone could judge, so it invites cynicism; the rewrite names a specific, checkable cause outside the lead's control, owns the lead's own role, explains how people will be treated, and invites the questions that test whether the account was adequate."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Social accounts",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Give the explanation at the same moment as the bad news or the admission, before people fill the silence with their own story."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "State the real reason - the constraint, trade-off or goal that drove the outcome - in concrete terms rather than \"business reasons\"."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Separate honestly what was outside your control from what was your call, and own your part; never invent a mitigating factor."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Say how the decision will be carried out and how the people affected will be treated, not only why it was made."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Make the detail proportional to the loss, then ask what still does not make sense and answer it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/social-accounts/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "If you caused the harm, put the account inside an apology - responsibility and repair first, explanation kept short."
  },
